      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T17:18:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@smostafa@google.com let\u0027s use the pKVM ABI to define this API.\n\nDoes \"success\" simply mean that there exists a region of `size` bytes starting at `base_ipa` that\u0027s mapped to a physical MMIO region? Or does the match need to be exact e.g. if there exist a region of `0x2000` bytes at `0x10000`, does `request_mmio(0x11000, 0x1000)` succeed?\n\nAlso, must `size` be a multiple of the (stage-2?) page size? What if there are 2 contiguous 2KiB regions in the same page? Does the hypervisor expect a single call per page?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2eae56d633800d37681ef2fca25b44d180a51a4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9c40f06_8bd2847a",
        "filename": "libs/hyp/src/hypervisor/common.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 83,
      "author": {
        "id": 1965911
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-20T17:33:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This function should return a token and not just success, as the token is an address it would be page aligned, so we can use SMCCC return values to return failures.\nI think it would be better to change that and return 2 values, an error code and the token if error code \u003d\u003d 0.\n\nRegarding the size, currently, the function must pass the range as seen in the device tree (per `regs` value), which is expected to be `PAGE_SIZE` aligned.\n\nIf we have a resource less than that, so this device can\u0027t be assigned.",
      "parentUuid": "ce5a145d_a1beb611",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 46,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "2eae56d633800d37681ef2fca25b44d180a51a4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
